.DS_Store

# ── Obsidian ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ignore vault config by default, then un-ignore the files that make a fresh
# clone reproducible. community-plugins.json is here deliberately: without it a
# clone gets every plugin's code and Obsidian enables none of it. That was the
# single biggest reproducibility gap in the workspace this template came from.
# The saved views are not here: they live in Obsidian/Views/ as ordinary vault
# files, because a view nobody can reach from the file explorer is not a view.
**/.obsidian/*
!**/.obsidian/plugins/
!**/.obsidian/themes/
!**/.obsidian/snippets/
!**/.obsidian/app.json
!**/.obsidian/community-plugins.json
!**/.obsidian/core-plugins.json

# Store-installed plugins are ignored wholesale, then the two that have to
# travel are named back in. A blanket rule rather than a list of ids, because a
# list only protects the plugins someone remembered to add to it: Templater and
# Excalidraw are AGPL-3.0, and a `git add -A` after installing either from
# Obsidian's browser would commit copyleft binaries into an MIT tree, which is
# the exact thing not vendoring them exists to prevent.
#
# agentic-copilot is vendored: MIT, not in the store, installable no other way.
#
# templater-obsidian is not vendored, but two files inside it are, because
# without them Templater arrives unconfigured and every template throws. Its
# built main.js stays ignored. See that folder's SETUP.md.
.obsidian/plugins/*/
!.obsidian/plugins/agentic-copilot/
!.obsidian/plugins/templater-obsidian/
.obsidian/plugins/templater-obsidian/*
!.obsidian/plugins/templater-obsidian/data.json.example
!.obsidian/plugins/templater-obsidian/SETUP.md

# Per-machine plugin state. Each machine writes its own from the .example file
# beside it, via `./workspace obsidian-setup`. See each plugin's SETUP.md.
#   agentic-copilot  data.json is a local preference file, and editApprovalMode
#                    is a security choice that should not arrive from a clone.
#   templater        data.json is covered by the blanket rule above.
.obsidian/plugins/agentic-copilot/data.json

# Themes are store-installed. The template ships no theme selection, so there is
# nothing here to travel.
.obsidian/themes/

# Per-machine pane layout. Also leaks the working set via lastOpenFiles.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json

# ── Credentials ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Commit only the scaffold: folder structure, .example templates, READMEs. A
# fresh clone gets a ready-to-fill skeleton and never a secret.
.credentials/**
!.credentials/**/
!.credentials/README.md
!.credentials/**/*.example
!.credentials/**/README.md
!.credentials/**/.gitkeep

# ── Harness runtime ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.scratchpad/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees
node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/.venv-*/
**/renderer/dist/
